  "qualification": "Eight shared public groups and one internal face-admission regression extend the retained corpus. BRep/IO release suites pass 707 all-feature and 699 minimal-feature tests. Affected all-target strict Clippy, warning-denied rustdoc, fuzz-target compilation and formatting pass. Source-path native consumers execute 115 groups plus eight original exchange workflows; actual zero-import WASM executes 253 groups, including all nine original exports. All 610 prior native archives re-encode byte-identically; 159 STEP inputs import 173 bodies and replay. The 785-file inventory has 408 distinct contents; text controls are inventory-only. All 308 fresh baseline/candidate pairs remain byte-identical, with no coefficient encoding migration. Every export recipe repeats deterministically; 22 new rotation/revolution archive files (12 distinct encodings) also replay stably. The initial copied-consumer root error is retained and corrected; its mis-scoped baseline result is excluded.",
  "costs": "Three alternating pairs cover 99 preserved semantic rows; eight new groups have three absolute trials. All 63 processes pass their assertions. Observed time ratios range 0.786806 to 1.271032; 5 exceed the 10% review marker and 2 increase allocation calls or requested bytes. All adverse observations are retained. Shared-host instrumented samples and process RSS establish neither a general speedup nor internal work/heap bounds.",
  "limits": "Finite retained circular orbits and selected open revolution sheets, with complete boundary-image and profile-axis-clearance proofs. No general rank-two surface regularity, embedding, solid closure or new STEP claim. Independent selected angular/axial parameters, retained vector derivatives, general affine orbit transport and inverse/intersection families remain typed frontiers. Schema 10 gains an additive Rotation record; existing corpus bytes are preserved, with no compatibility reader. Total work, retained heap, coefficient growth, cancellation, runtime fuzz/ASan/lexicase, formal coverage, MSRV, installed distributions and production binding gates remain open. All 28 work packages remain open/in-progress. Full pre-push qualification remains required; the consumed eaa0 one-time exception does not authorize publishing this increment.",
